---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'

import { Button, Timeline } from 'astro-pure/user'
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/CommonPage.astro'
import prao from '@/assets/prao.png'

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'about', text: 'About me' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'tools', text: 'Favourite sci-fi books' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'about-this-blog', text: 'About this blog' },
]
---

<PageLayout title='' {headings} info='/about'>
  <h2 id='about'>About me</h2>
  <main class='flex w-full flex-col items-center'>
    <Image
      src={prao}
      alt='prao'
      class='h-48 w-auto rounded-full border p-1'
      ='eager'
    />    
  </main>
  <p>
    I'm an AI engineer and researcher who's passionate about building intelligent,automated applications
    using agents and the tools around them. My interests vary over time but largely combine insights from
    data modelling, knowledge graphs, machine learning, data infrastructure and agentic systems. 
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm based in Toronto 🇨🇦, and have previously lived in Vancouver 🇨🇦, London 🇬🇧 and Ann Arbor,
    Michigan 🇺🇸. I love writing technical content and digging into the internals of the various tools and
    frameworks in the AI and data ecosystem, and I'm always dabbling in or building something new in
    Python 🐍 and Rust 🦀. I'm a huge proponent of open source software and open knowledge-sharing, both
    in person and through my writing in this blog.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    I'm a fan of hard sci-fi, and have a soft spot for books that feature space exploration,
    interplanetary travel and other deep physics themes that allow us to dream about the limits of what's possible.
    In my spare time, I enjoy hiking, biking, exploring nature and trying out new teas.
    If you like what you're reading here, consider buying me a coffee/tea using the button below!
  </p>
  <Button title='Buy me a coffee or tea' class='w-fit' href='https://buymeacoffee.com/prrao87' style='ahead' />

  {/* general-talk */}
  <h2 id='books'>Favourite sci-fi books</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><i>The Three-body Problem</i>, by Cixin Liu</li>
    <li><i>The Dark Forest</i>, by Cixin Liu</li>
    <li><i>Death's End</i>, by Cixin Liu</li>
    <li><i>Aurora</i>, by Kim Stanley Robinson</li>
  </ul>

    Reach out to me <a href='https://x.com/tech_optimist'>on X</a> to recommend some excellent hard sci-fi
    books of this calibre!

  {/* gossips 
  <h2 id='gossips'>Gossips</h2>
  <Collapse title='Lorem ipsum'>
    Any specific gossip here
  </Collapse>
  */}

  {/* about-this-blog */}
  <h2 id='about-this-blog'>About this blog</h2>
  <p>What began as a personal journey of writing down my learnings eventually led to this blog finding
  enthusiastic readers from all over the planet! 🌎 </p>
  <Timeline
    events={[
      {
        date: '2023-04-29',
        content:
          'Initial "Hello World" blog post on this site, powered by Hugo'
      },
      {
        date: '2023-11-30',
        content:
          'Updated blog site powered by Zola, using the Serene theme'
      },
      {
        date: '2025-02-25',
        content: 'Revamp of this site to use Astro Pure theme'
      }
    ]}
  />
  Many thanks to all readers who read my posts, and to all those who've indulged with me in nerdy
  technical discussions over the years!
</PageLayout>
